@section 18.5 | Tourism and Trade Relations

@q 12:79-82

@src1 12:10
@one U.P.P.C.S. (Mains) 2013
According to report of U.N. World Tourism Organization (2010) the most visited country in the world is
@ans France
@end

**France** is still the most visited country. Indians travelled most to **Singapore** in 2010, but the **UAE** leads now (about 25% of Indian trips abroad). Foreign tourist arrivals fell in **2009** (global crisis) and in **2020-21** (COVID). **Udaipur** was voted the world's best city by *Travel + Leisure* in 2009.

@q 12:83-86

**Nathu La** (Sikkim) reopened for border trade with **China** in **2006**. The **India International Trade Fair 2021** was held at **Pragati Maidan, New Delhi** (not Jaipur), with the theme "**Atmanirbhar Bharat**".

@up UP link: **Noida SEZ** (1985) is one of India's original EPZs. Under FTP 2023, **Mirzapur** (carpets), **Moradabad** (handicrafts) and **Varanasi** (handlooms) became "Towns of Export Excellence". UP's ODOP products are the base of its district export plans.

@trap
**Invisible export = services.** **Entrepot = import for re-export.** **Tariff reduces trade.** **Duty drawback = refund of import duty.** **FTP 2023: no end date, US$ 2 trillion by 2030.** **Kandla 1965 first EPZ in Asia; Surat first private EPZ.** **SEZ policy April 2000; Act 2005, in force 2006.** **EXIM Bank 1982; ECGC = export insurance; IBEF 1996; MPEDA 1972, Kochi.** **France = most visited.** **Nathu La = China (2006).** **Panna = diamonds.**
@end

@heatmap

@pattern
SEZ and EPZ facts were asked repeatedly from 1999 to 2017; the **2021-2023** papers added promotion bodies (MPEDA, Falta EPZ) and trade fairs. Basic terms (tariff, entrepot, duty drawback) are perennial.
@end

